---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const description =
  "Baron Hines is a software developer on SailPoint's Non-Employee Platform team.";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={description}>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="muted">My name is Baron Hines. I write software for a living, and I've been hooked on it since I was a kid.</p>

  <ul class="project-links">
    <li>
      <a class="repo-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/baronhines/">
        {/* A plain "in" in a box, drawn in the text color so it follows the theme. Not LinkedIn's logo. */}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="20" rx="3" />
          <circle cx="7" cy="7.5" r="1.1" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
          <path d="M7 10.5v7" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <path d="M11 17.5v-7M11 13.5c0-1.8 1.2-3 2.8-3s2.7 1.1 2.7 3v4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
        LinkedIn
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="repo-link" href="https://github.com/baron-hines">
        {/* GitHub's mark (Primer Octicons "mark-github", MIT), as on the project pages. */}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true">
          <path fill="currentColor" d="M8 0c4.42 0 8 3.58 8 8a8.013 8.013 0 0 1-5.45 7.59c-.4.08-.55-.17-.55-.38 0-.27.01-1.13.01-2.2 0-.75-.25-1.23-.54-1.48 1.78-.2 3.65-.88 3.65-3.95 0-.88-.31-1.59-.82-2.15.08-.2.36-1.02-.08-2.12 0 0-.67-.22-2.2.82-.64-.18-1.32-.27-2-.27-.68 0-1.36.09-2 .27-1.53-1.03-2.2-.82-2.2-.82-.44 1.1-.16 1.92-.08 2.12-.51.56-.82 1.28-.82 2.15 0 3.06 1.86 3.75 3.64 3.95-.23.2-.44.55-.51 1.07-.46.21-1.61.55-2.33-.66-.15-.24-.6-.83-1.23-.82-.67.01-.27.38.01.53.34.19.73.9.82 1.13.16.45.68 1.31 2.69.94 0 .67.01 1.3.01 1.49 0 .21-.15.45-.55.38A7.995 7.995 0 0 1 0 8c0-4.42 3.58-8 8-8Z" />
        </svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <p>
      I work on SailPoint's <a href="https://www.sailpoint.com/products/non-employee-risk-management">Non-Employee Platform</a>, making it extensible, performant, and easy to monitor. That
      means the environments, the tooling, and the shared code the rest of the team builds on. This ensures our
      developers focus on business logic instead of re-inventing patterns.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside work</h2>
    <p>
      Fargo, North Dakota has given me a forced love of snow removal. I'll happily talk about snow blowers, snow
      fences, or drifts taller than I am.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of my free time goes to cars. I race online sims, follow Formula 1, autocross, and I'm learning to be a
      mechanic. I'm always trying to learn something new.
    </p>
    {/* One line on purpose: Astro drops the space at a line break next to a link. */}
    <p>I also code for fun. At home I run a server with my own <a href="/projects/local-ai-stack/">AI stack</a> and the <a href="/projects/coding-stack/">coding stack</a> that ships it, and I write about both here. The <a href="/projects/">projects</a> page has what I'm working on now.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
